{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>ולא יבאו לראות כבלע את הקדש</b> – When they insert the vessel into its cover, as he explained above in this pericope: 'and they shall spread over it a garment of such-and-such, and cover it with a covering of such-and-such' — and its בליעה (swallowing) is its covering. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 4:20), and it is the view of Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Numbers 4:20). And our Rabbis said in tractate Sanhedrin (Sanhedrin 81a) that this is a warning against one who steals a sacred vessel, who is liable to death, and the zealous may strike him down, for theft and robbery are called בליעה (swallowing), from the language of 'חיל בלע ויקיאנו' (Job 20:15), 'והוצאתי את בלעו מפיו' (Jeremiah 51:44). And R. Abraham ibn Ezra (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 4:20) said according to its plain sense: that they shall not come to look when the curtain-screen is removed and the Ark is uncovered; only afterward, once it is covered, may they come to carry it. And <b>כבלע את הקדש</b> would mean when the structure is removed from upon the Ark, which is 'the holy' — from the language of 'בלע ה׳ ולא חמל' (Lamentations 2:2), 'יחד סביב ותבלעני' (Job 10:8). And behold, the Levites are warned not to touch the Ark of the Holy and die; rather, they shall carry it by the poles. And further He warns them not to come to look at the removal of the structure at all while Aaron takes down the curtain, as in the matter of 'כי ראו בארון ה׳' (I Samuel 6:19). And he spoke well. But by way of truth, the reason of the verse is that because the glory of the One enthroned upon the Cherubim is there, the Levites were warned not to presume to look upon YHWH until the priests take down the curtain, for then the Glory will appear in the hiddenness of His might and return to its first place, to the Holy of Holies, and כבלע את הקדש will be according to its plain sense, and the enlightened will understand:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "In the kabbalistic section, 'the glory of the One enthroned upon the Cherubim' renders כבוד יושב הכרובים; the cryptic concluding reference to the Glory returning to its first place is preserved without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:46.630110172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}